{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U8s3LuvBEhqnBnRD7ZCqzR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Context: the Shelf service\n2\t\n3\tA gRPC server (Go, `google.golang.org/grpc`) over a SQLite file. The contract is `proto/toy/v1/shelf.proto`; the\n4\tbehaviour is `REQUIREMENTS.md` / `spec.py`. You build the server; you do not change the proto, the spec, the harness,\n5\tthe generator or this file.\n6\t\n7\t* **Stubs.** `gen/toy/v1/*.pb.go` is produced by `./generate.sh` (buf) from the proto and is rebuilt by every\n8\t  `./check.sh`. Never write or edit anything under `gen/`. Import it as `toyv1 \"example.com/toybuild/gen/toy/v1\"`.\n9\t* **Entry point.** A `package main` at the repository root (`go build -o bin/toy-server .`).\n10\t* **Environment the checker sets.** `PORT`: listen for gRPC on `127.0.0.1:$PORT` (plaintext). `DB_PATH`: the SQLite file;\n11\t  the table `items(id integer primary key autoincrement, name text not null unique, qty integer not null)` already\n12\t  exists (the harness created it): do not create or migrate tables. Use `database/sql` with the pure-Go driver\n13\t  `modernc.org/sqlite` (driver name `\"sqlite\"`; open `file:<DB_PATH>?_pragma=busy_timeout(10000)` and\n14\t  `SetMaxOpenConns(1)`).\n15\t* **Readiness.** The checker waits for the standard health service (`google.golang.org/grpc/health`, registered on the\n16\t  same server) to answer `SERVING` for the empty service name.\n17\t* **Dependencies.** `go.mod` and `go.sum` already list what the build needs (grpc, protobuf, modernc sqlite, health).\n18\t  There is no network and no `go mod tidy` in the gate: use only packages those modules provide.\n19\t* **Gate.** `./check.sh` (generate, build, then the Lattice check of `spec.py`, layers C and D). Exit 0 = done.\n20\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"279da829-4183-4c7e-af87-b7ea8e7504b9","uuid":"1b644092-1432-4a9e-9630-d6382f03a4b6","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:29:43.571Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/fj/tl69n2xd067clrqbx31xtrtr0000gn/T/lo-pilot-tp_vbzcy/U-C/repo/CONTEXT.md","content":"# Context: the Shelf service\n\nA gRPC server (Go, `google.golang.org/grpc`) over a SQLite file. The contract is `proto/toy/v1/shelf.proto`; the\nbehaviour is `REQUIREMENTS.md` / `spec.py`. You build the server; you do not change the proto, the spec, the harness,\nthe generator or this file.\n\n* **Stubs.** `gen/toy/v1/*.pb.go` is produced by `./generate.sh` (buf) from the proto and is rebuilt by every\n  `./check.sh`. Never write or edit anything under `gen/`. Import it as `toyv1 \"example.com/toybuild/gen/toy/v1\"`.\n* **Entry point.** A `package main` at the repository root (`go build -o bin/toy-server .`).\n* **Environment the checker sets.** `PORT`: listen for gRPC on `127.0.0.1:$PORT` (plaintext). `DB_PATH`: the SQLite file;\n  the table `items(id integer primary key autoincrement, name text not null unique, qty integer not null)` already\n  exists (the harness created it): do not create or migrate tables. Use `database/sql` with the pure-Go driver\n  `modernc.org/sqlite` (driver name `\"sqlite\"`; open `file:<DB_PATH>?_pragma=busy_timeout(10000)` and\n  `SetMaxOpenConns(1)`).\n* **Readiness.** The checker waits for the standard health service (`google.golang.org/grpc/health`, registered on the\n  same server) to answer `SERVING` for the empty service name.\n* **Dependencies.** `go.mod` and `go.sum` already list what the build needs (grpc, protobuf, modernc sqlite, health).\n  There is no network and no `go mod tidy` in the gate: use only packages those modules provide.\n* **Gate.** `./check.sh` (generate, build, then the Lattice check of `spec.py`, layers C and D). Exit 0 = done.\n","numLines":20,"startLine":1,"totalLines":20}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01U8s3LuvBEhqnBnRD7ZCqzR","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QPJQX7qtjhftCiWHhPPfqD","type":"tool_result","content":"CONTEXT.md\nREQUIREMENTS.md\nbuf.gen.yaml\nbuf.yaml\ncheck.sh\ngen\ngenerate.sh\ngo.mod\ngo.sum\nharness.py\nmain.go\nproto\npyproject.toml\nshelf.go\nspec.py\nspec.trace.json\nstudio.toml\n\n./gen:\ntoy\n\n./gen/toy:\nv1\n\n./gen/toy/v1:\nshelf.pb.go\nshelf_grpc.pb.go\n\n./proto:\ntoy\n\n./proto/toy:\nv1\n\n./proto/toy/v1:\nshelf.proto\n#!/bin/sh\n# The gate: build the server, check it against spec.py (layers C and D). The stubs in gen/ come from\n# `[grpc] generate` in studio.toml, which the loop runs before this gate (round 5, L2); run ./generate.sh by hand outside it.\n# Exit 0 = clean. LATTICE_REBUILD set (Studio running this as a gate) also writes metrics/last-check.json.\nset -e\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\"\nmkdir -p bin\ngo build -o bin/toy-server .\nset -- --spec spec:SPEC --app harness:make_app --db harness:build_db --runtime harness:RUNTIME --layers CD \"$@\"\nif [ -n \"${LATTICE_REBUILD:-}\" ] || [ \"${TOY_CHECK_JSON:-0}\" = \"1\" ]; then\n  mkdir -p metrics\n  set +e\n  uv run python -m lattice.spec check \"$@\" --json > metrics/last-check.json\n  rc=$?\n  set -e\n  uv run python -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('metrics/last-check.json')); print(json.dumps({k: d[k] for k in d if k not in ('cases','findings')}, indent=1)[:3000])\" || true\n  exit $rc\nfi\nexec uv run python -m lattice.spec check \"$@\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"279da829-4183-4c7e-af87-b7ea8e7504b9","uuid":"a7a8b2d0-f4ac-4730-9371-6b355e6c2884","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:29:43.616Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"CONTEXT.md\nREQUIREMENTS.md\nbuf.gen.yaml\nbuf.yaml\ncheck.sh\ngen\ngenerate.sh\ngo.mod\ngo.sum\nharness.py\nmain.go\nproto\npyproject.toml\nshelf.go\nspec.py\nspec.trace.json\nstudio.toml\n\n./gen:\ntoy\n\n./gen/toy:\nv1\n\n./gen/toy/v1:\nshelf.pb.go\nshelf_grpc.pb.go\n\n./proto:\ntoy\n\n./proto/toy:\nv1\n\n./proto/toy/v1:\nshelf.proto\n#!/bin/sh\n# The gate: build the server, check it against spec.py (layers C and D). The stubs in gen/ come from\n# `[grpc] generate` in studio.toml, which the loop runs before this gate (round 5, L2); run ./generate.sh by hand outside it.\n# Exit 0 = clean. LATTICE_REBUILD set (Studio running this as a gate) also writes metrics/last-check.json.\nset -e\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\"\nmkdir -p bin\ngo build -o bin/toy-server .\nset -- --spec spec:SPEC --app harness:make_app --db harness:build_db --runtime harness:RUNTIME --layers CD \"$@\"\nif [ -n \"${LATTICE_REBUILD:-}\" ] || [ \"${TOY_CHECK_JSON:-0}\" = \"1\" ]; then\n  mkdir -p metrics\n  set +e\n  uv run python -m lattice.spec check \"$@\" --json > metrics/last-check.json\n  rc=$?\n  set -e\n  uv run python -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('metrics/last-check.json')); print(json.dumps({k: d[k] for k in d if k not in ('cases','findings')}, indent=1)[:3000])\" || true\n  exit $rc\nfi\nexec uv run python -m lattice.spec check \"$@\"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QPJQX7qtjhftCiWHhPPfqD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"subcommandResults"}}]}
