{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb2XVcd5EraRr1QN5BNi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I implemented all four Shelf RPCs in `shelf.go`, but I couldn't run `./check.sh` after the change. Bash was denied in this session, so nothing has been built or checked.\n\nRules R9 and R10 contradict each other. R9 says `GetItem` never creates or changes a row. R10 says a missing item must register a \"ghost\" row. The scenario `get_registers_ghost` also fails on its own terms: Studio's check says no earlier step writes a \"ghost\" row, so no implementation can satisfy it. I followed R9, so `GetItem` returns NOT_FOUND without writing, and `get_registers_ghost` will keep failing until the owner fixes the spec.\n\nAdd, get, list and remove follow R1–R7. Add refuses an empty name or a negative quantity with INVALID_ARGUMENT, and a duplicate name with ALREADY_EXISTS. List returns items ordered by id."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1560,"cache_read_input_tokens":17815,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1560},"output_tokens":306,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"279da829-4183-4c7e-af87-b7ea8e7504b9","uuid":"1559e9b6-f200-4bc7-ab45-3ef8260f4890","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:30:08.862Z","request_id":"req_011Cgb2XVSCgQa7w67egzzbg"}
